{"seq":16,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:23:58.981Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"9fe836460baeda8425aaa30d360ae5c2bfd56b928a0ee53d913e85df350515da","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina Kroll, here's what I found for Kwame's account review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests/cheat sheet. Pellow Home Living is left out.\n\n*Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)*\n• Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Still open per Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n• No ticket number: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change is listed as the main friction point (cheat sheet).\n\n*Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF, Puget Sound)*\n• Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers (cheat sheet).\n• Ticket #4419: barge slip 7 schedule sync, on Kwame's port account (Moss's 11/2/2025 digest). They also asked for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift.\n• No ticket number: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch (cheat sheet).\n\n*Please check:* #4419 appears under both accounts. The cheat sheet puts it on PHL (Yard_Dwell_Summary timeout). The 11/2 digest puts it on the port account with Driftmoor (barge slip 7 sync). I can't tell from these sources which is right, or whether it's two different tickets sharing a number. Kwame can probably confirm.\n\n*Left out:* PD-4821 and #8812 (Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark), and PD-4827 and PD-4824 (Saltmarsh Provisions).\n\n*Outside the sources you named:* your public note from 2025-12-08 mentions PD-8841 on PHL (chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B, Beaumont barge slip). I didn't count it in the list above, but it's PHL if you want it added.\n\nThe channels and notes only show tickets people mentioned. I didn't look at the ticketing system itself, so this may not be everything.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T02:24:04.016Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"89347b2317cf7bfe5829a358d19f6c43c59f1d82ee5a4f0d1d30701e477ae797","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I posted the list as a reply in your #coastal-team thread. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet, and left Pellow Home Living out.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics**\n- Ticket #4419: the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It is still open.\n- No ticket number: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change is listed as the main friction point.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight**\n- Feature request #882: a bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- Ticket #4419: barge slip 7 schedule sync, plus a request for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift.\n- No ticket number: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch.\n\n**Ticket #4419 needs checking.** Moss's cheat sheet puts it on PHL (the report timeout). Moss's 11/2/2025 digest puts it on Kwame's port account with Driftmoor (barge slip 7). I can't tell which is right, or whether two tickets share the number. Kwame can probably confirm.\n\n**Left out:** PD-4821 and #8812 (Pellow Home Living) and PD-4827 and PD-4824 (Saltmarsh Provisions).\n\n**Outside the sources you asked for:** your public note from 2025-12-08 mentions PD-8841 on PHL (chassis pool holds, Gate 4B). I didn't count it in the list, but it belongs there if you want it added.\n\nI only had the channels and notes, not the ticketing system itself, so this may not be every ticket."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
